{"assets":["/statement-assets/468b8852aa57a3661779afa31b3db830044a5ecd4d7f9d0687d9468104bd819a.png","/statement-assets/24b0d025e24a609ba50c7706118460d93e2633c16bba9066497a0f9bcd9f146b.png","/statement-assets/06a3819fe43fb00e6d5a0790c7f3370b305164b3dcf71ecd0096c213fb139357.png","/statement-assets/a5e34dca8140f725d206df74f675eee5ebdcfde3b787b17d9145182bd0b1d256.png","/statement-assets/64e41df9d5965ab39630717ed79117c940f80fd0234d19fdccc7125687c4cd66.png","/statement-assets/2ef8e41989d4f11650a994056f22fbf37d32c34a3a5d1f9ad93fe748a077f475.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"183","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Cyclic Coloring"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"directed"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" arcs ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"multiple arcs and self-loops"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are allowed). You have to paint each vertex of the graph into one of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(k ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" colors in such way that for all arcs of the graph leading from a vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" to vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":", vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" is painted with the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next color"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the color used to paint vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The colors are numbered cyclically "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":". This means that for each color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i < k)"},{"kind":"text","text":" its next color is color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". In addition, the next color of color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" is color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note, that if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the next color for color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is again color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find and print the largest possible value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(k ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that it's possible to color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" as described above with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" colors. Note that you don't necessarily use all the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" colors (that is, for each color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" there does not necessarily exist a vertex that is colored with color "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":"), denoting the number of vertices and the number of arcs of the given digraph, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines follow, each line will contain two space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai, bi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), which means that the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th arc goes from vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" to vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Multiple arcs and self-loops are allowed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the maximum possible number of the colors that can be used to paint the digraph (i.e. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", as described in the problem statement). Note that the desired value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" must satisfy the inequality "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],